module lib/hf/tests/boys
  The checks of lib/hf/boys against reference data, and their helpers.

boys_worst_member  @ee8fe29f
  why   The measurement behind the accuracy tests: one number per member and
        top order, with where it happened so a failure can be found.
  k     the member's index in boys_methods
  nmax  the top order to evaluate at
  ms    the registry
  T     the mpmath table, one row per tabulated `x`
  X     the tabulated arguments
  worst the worst relative error so far
  wx    the `x` index where it happened
  wn    the order where it happened
  F     the member's values at one tabulated argument
  rel   the relative error of one order

boys_worst_grid  @df93c5fb
  why   The same measurement for a grid built once, which is how production
        callers use it.
  nmax   the top order
  G      the grid, built up to `BOYS_T_GRID_XMAX`
  worst  the largest relative error so far

boys_zero_gap  @7638009c
  why   At $x = 0$ the function is exactly $1/(2n+1)$, a check that needs no
        table [test "every member gives 1/(2n+1) at x = 0"].
  k      the member's index
  F      its values at zero
  exact  $1/(2n+1)$
  worst  the largest relative gap so far

boys_table_index  @b92bb5d3
  why   The switch tests look up the table rows on each side of a switch by
        their argument.
  x      the argument to find
  found  its row, or `-1`
